## 1.13.1
- Map: a changed region is no longer drawn again in full; only the chunks saved since its last drawing are (the region file keeps a time per chunk), plus their neighbours for the relief. The game saves the regions around players over and over, so this saves most of the panel's map work on a busy server and during pregeneration
- Market: the copy for the info page isn't written again every 15 seconds when nothing changed
- Navbar: the CPU tile shows the server's CPU in cores too ("≈ 3.4 of 12 cores"), comparable to docker stats (which counts 100 % per core); needs mod 1.14.1
- The mod's pages in the frame pause their updates while one of the panel's own pages is shown

## 1.13.0
- Home: the greeting and the "running smoothly" card are one card (health, time window, version and mods); online state and the clock aren't repeated (they're at the top); available updates aren't listed under Needs attention
- Navbar: a pill next to the game clock while chunks are being pregenerated ("Overworld: 42%"), click it for World → Borders; the Players tile shows the player limit; the GC tile shows the number its colour comes from
- Sidebar: Players counts who's online without opening the page first; the unexplained number on Server is gone
- Console: timestamps on the panel's own lines and command echoes; the Panel filter is part of Nice Control Center; the console reconnects on its own when the connection went quiet (no more reloading the page)
- Players: the player list runs as long as the open player card
- Gameplay: Better Mending (Items & tools); hide ores from x-ray and crops in the rain (World & nature); AFK players don't count for sleeping (Chat & tab list) — needs mod 1.14.0
- Tuning: tick-less and lighter-AI ranges are set as a share of the simulation distance (mod 1.14.0)
- Map: waypoint hub pins in the colour of the hub's title, with the hub's own head; with "names of who's online" the status card always lists them ("nobody right now" otherwise) and a name jumps to that player
- Market and info page: shulker boxes, chests, banners and other items the game draws with code get icons
- Files: downloading a single file (like a .log.gz) no longer fails with "Insufficient content written"
- Startup & Java: "Memory right now" shows what the Minecraft process, the panel and the container use, with the file cache the system gives back on its own
- Docker: the panel's own Java has a fixed 1.5 GB heap limit (was 25 % of the host's memory); PANEL_JAVA_OPTS changes it
- Database: market_mail (what waits in each player's market mailbox) and pets_owned (who owns which pet) for the website; one broken market entry no longer stops the whole copy

